.* PROBLEM2: the task menu for more problem handling.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='PROBLEM2'.
:IMPORT NAME=STRDBG PNLGRP=QHDBGCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKCNTINF PNLGRP=QHSXCMD.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS HELP='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F13 ACTION='MENU INFO'.F13=Information Assistant
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='MENU MAIN'.F16=System Main menu
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=PROBLEM2 HELP=HLPPROBLEM2 KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.Problem Handling
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='MENU PTF' HELP='PROBLEM2/OPT1'.Program temporary fix
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD WRKALR' HELP='PROBLEM2/OPT2'.Work with alerts
:MENUI OPTION=3 ACTION='MENU PERFORM' HELP='PROBLEM2/OPT3'.Performance tools
:MENUI OPTION=4 ACTION='CMD ?STRDBG' HELP=STRDBG.Programming language debug
:MENUI OPTION=5 ACTION='CMD WRKCNTINF' HELP=WRKCNTINF.Work with support contact information
:MENUI OPTION=6 ACTION='CMD ?STRCPYSCN' HELP='PROBLEM2/OPT6'.Copy screen image
:MENUI OPTION=7 ACTION='CMD WRKALRD' HELP='PROBLEM2/OPT7'.Work with alert descriptions
:MENUI OPTION=70 ACTION='MENU CMDPRB' HELP='PROBLEM2/OPT70'.Related commands
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPPROBLEM2.Problem Handling - Help
:P.The second page of problem handling: fixes, alerts, performance and
debugging.
:P.Type an option number or a command and press Enter. F4 prompts the
command, F9 brings the previous one back, F12 returns to the menu shown
before this one.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F13=Information Assistant
:PD.Shows menu INFO.
:PT.F16=System Main menu
:PD.Shows menu MAIN.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PROBLEM2/OPT1'.Program temporary fix
:P.Option 1. Shows menu PTF&colon. Program temporary fix.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PROBLEM2/OPT2'.Work with alerts
:P.Option 2. Runs the WRKALR command&colon. Work with alerts.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PROBLEM2/OPT3'.Performance tools
:P.Option 3. Shows menu PERFORM&colon. Performance tools.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PROBLEM2/OPT6'.Copy screen image
:P.Option 6. Runs the STRCPYSCN command&colon. Copy screen image.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PROBLEM2/OPT7'.Work with alert descriptions
:P.Option 7. Runs the WRKALRD command&colon. Work with alert
descriptions.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PROBLEM2/OPT70'.Related commands
:P.Option 70. Shows menu CMDPRB&colon. Related commands.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
